      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "so since I made this suggestion, the way the social status works was changed. but it still doesn't entirely address the problem. As is it's just a blanket \"all can join\" or \"all must request/cannot join\"\nit would be nice to be able to keep certain friend groups separate. In real life, its easy to keep friend groups separate, since you have to actively physically go to them, you dont have instant gps teleportation.\nThe way the social tab currently is, with the favorites section, it would be nice if there was something similar, where you could assign friends into personal groupings, and simply apply the social statuses to that. so group A might be set to green, group B to orange, etc",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-11T18:11:34.091Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "At a certain point, you start having multiple friend groups, which is nice, but sometimes you dont want a whole lot of crossover between the different groups. So while I know that \"guilds\" idea has been floating around for a while, this is more an abstract request for something sort of like how Friends Only works, or how the red status works in private maps.\n\nPlenty of times Ill try and use the red status when i dont want people to join, but people end up doing so anyway, which can lead to a chain reaction. Maybe something so that when your status is red you *cannot* be joined off of?\n\nI dont really have a proper suggestion here, just a general request for something of that nature for this particular issue",
